```json
{
  "calls": [
    {
      "tool": "tracker.create",
      "args": {
        "title": "cache eviction storm",
        "severity": "S3",
        "component": "billing",
        "assignee": "dana",
        "due_date": "2026-08-26"
      }
    },
    {
      "tool": "mail.send",
      "args": {
        "to": ["sre@corp.example"],
        "cc": [],
        "subject": "cache eviction storm S3",
        "body": "Filed S3 tracker ticket 'cache eviction storm' (ticket id: {{ticket_id}}). Component: billing. Assignee: dana. Due date: 2026-08-26.",
        "priority": "high"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Notes on resolution:
- **Due Wednesday**: Today is Monday 2026-08-24, so Wednesday resolves to **2026-08-26**.
- **Ticket ID**: Not specified anywhere in the source — it is generated by `tracker.create` at execution time. The email body therefore uses the placeholder `{{ticket_id}}`, which must be replaced with the actual ticket id returned by the first call before sending. This is why ordering matters (tracker.create must complete before mail.send).
- All other parameters (title, severity S3, component billing, assignee dana, recipient sre@corp.example, subject 'cache eviction storm S3', priority high) are taken directly from the request; no cc recipients were specified, so cc is empty.
